Aim:-
Write a program demonstate tuple & related functions in python

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Create three tuples:
    t1 = (1, 2, 3)
    t2 = (230, 36, 200)
    t3 = ("Apples", "Banana", "Watermelon", "Dragon Fruit")
3. Display the original tuples t1, t2, t3
4. Display the first element of t1
5. Display the second element of t2
6. Display the third element of t3
7. Find and display the length of t1
8. Find and display the length of t2
9. Find and display the length of t3
10. Create a nested tuple using t1 and t3 and display it
11. Concatenate t2 and t3 to create t4
12. Display t4
13. Check whether 2 is present in t1 and display the result
14. Check whether "mango" is present in t3 and display the result
15. Input a fruit name word from the user
16. If word is present in t3, display that it is present
17. Otherwise display that it is not present
18. Create a tuple numbers = (98, 28, 23, 10, 4, 10, 48, 84, 19)
19. Find and display the maximum value in numbers
20. Find and display the minimum value in numbers
21. Find and display the sum of all values in numbers
22. End

Code:-
t1 = (1, 2, 3)
t2 = (230, 36, 200)
t3 = ("Apples", "Banana", "Watermelon", "Dragon Fruit")

print("Original Tuple:", t1, t2, t3)

print("First element of t1:", t1[0])
print("Second element of t2:", t2[1])
print("Third element of t3:", t3[2])

print("Length of tuple 1:", len(t1))
print("Length of tuple 2:", len(t2))
print("Length of tuple 3:", len(t3))

nested_tuple = (t1, t3)
print("Nested Tuple:", nested_tuple)

t4 = t2 + t3
print("Concatenation of t2 and t3:", t4)
print("-" * 20)

print("Is 2 in t1?", 2 in t1)
print("Is mango in t3?", "mango" in t3)

word = input("Enter a fruit name to check: ")
if word in t3:
    print(word, "is present in tuple")
else:
    print(word, "is not present in tuple")

numbers = (98, 28, 23, 10, 4, 10, 48, 84, 19)
print("Max value:", max(numbers))
print("Min value:", min(numbers))
print("Sum of value:", sum(numbers))

